Hi [~accountid:5e343c77a7f27d0e6c6d6698] - thanks for confirming!

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
We’ve discussed this internally within the Privacy team and agreed that this topic will be addressed separately together with the *Billing* and *Identity* teams as part of the ongoing *Data Retention Mapping* project. Our understanding is that the *Identity team has already engaged with Billing* on this topic, so we suggest continuing coordination through that process.

Preliminary, will *not single out individual data points* from invoices (e.g., names, contact details) for retention purposes. Instead, we’ll focus on *mapping the retention of the invoice documents as a whole*, based on applicable *legal requirements* and *business purposes*. The general retention principles remain as outlined earlier in this ticket - our goal is to ensure full visibility into the underlying legal and business purposes for retention.
{panel}

Please let us know if you have any questions. Otherwise, we’re planning to *close this ticket* accordingly.

