The issue is because the Targeting values are not received by the time the endpoint is called. In the [AccessTokenInterceptor|https://github.com/bolteu/android-app-client/blob/b5457807a95fa37ca7ab913526ee82d0d2527140/modules/network/network-config/src/main/java/eu/bolt/networkconfig/interceptors/AccessTokenInterceptor.kt#L24-L30] there is a check for the {{JWTAuth}} feature flag value:

{noformat}val accessToken = getAccessJwtTokenUseCase.execute()
val shouldUseJwtAuth = targetingManager.get(Experiment.BoolExperiment.JWTAuth)
val request = chain.request().newBuilder()
if (shouldUseJwtAuth && accessToken != null) {
    request.addHeader(NetworkConsts.AUTH_HEADER_NAME, "${NetworkConsts.TOKEN_TYPE} $accessToken")
} else {
    addAuthHeaderIfPossible(request)
}{noformat}

The default value is {{false}}, so even though the {{accessToken}} is not {{null}} the interceptor forces the {{/comms/voip/register}} to use {{Basic}} instead of {{Bearer}} but for the {{Basic}} authentication header there is no value either (maybe it is not set yet).

