h3. Suggested Legal Insertions in the Special Terms

h4. *1. Payments*

{quote}The Parties agree on the following *Service Fee of Bolt Business structure*, based on monthly consumption:

* 0% fee for the first 4 months;
* 10% fee up to €10,000;
* 7.5% fee from €10,001 to €20,000;
* 3% fee from €20,001 to €35,000;
* 0% fee above €35,000.{quote}

h4. *2. Rebate*

{quote}The Customer shall receive a *monthly rebate*, calculated on the total monthly consumption of Bolt Services as follows:

* Up to €50,000 → 0% rebate;
* €50,000–€70,000 → 1%;
* €70,000–€80,000 → 1.5%;
* €80,000–€90,000 → 2%;
* €90,000–€95,000 → 3%;
* Above €95,000 → 5% (includes exclusivity until March 2026).
Rebates are credited in the invoice of the following month.{quote}



h3. *Rebate Logic*

Within Bolt Business, we can apply a *commercial rebate* mechanism — effectively a *volume-based discount* tied to the customer’s total monthly consumption (in this case, coupon usage).

In practice, this means:

* The client (Coverflex) consumes a certain total value of Bolt services each month through their account (mainly via coupons).
* Based on that monthly volume, Bolt grants a *percentage discount (rebate)* according to predefined thresholds.
* The *rebate is not applied immediately* — instead, it is *credited in the following month’s invoice* as a deduction (e.g. “Rebate for consumption in October”).

Example:
If Coverflex’s users consume €95,000 in Bolt coupons in one month, they reach the 5% rebate tier.
In the next month’s invoice, Bolt issues a *€4,750 credit (5%)* against that consumption as a *commercial discount*.

This structure rewards higher usage and allows flexible commercial management without changing the product pricing itself.





h4. *3. Exclusivity*

{quote}Until March 2026, Bolt shall be the *exclusive mobility partner* integrated in the Coverflex platform.
{quote}

h4. *4. Term*

{quote}This Agreement is valid for twelve (12) months from the Go-Live Date and *renews automatically* unless either Party provides thirty (30) days’ written notice of non-renewal.{quote}

