Thanks [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] - appreciate it. 🙂 

My main concern here / issue I am trying to resolve is whether to classify the kiosk provider as an independent controller or as a processor on Bolt’s behalf.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
* *Argument (A) - Kiosk provider as a processor*: Seeing as the kiosk provider effectively provides the Bolt interface and does not decide on what data to collect / for what purposes (i.e., the passenger input the data, according to textboxes determined by Bolt), I am struggling to understand why this party would not be acting as a processor on Bolt’s behalf (I cannot even find a privacy notice for this kiosk provider online, so I doubt they would be presenting themselves as a controller to the passenger). I also assume it would be helpful for Bolt to keep the kiosk provider on a tight leash by implementing processor-like restrictions on what the kiosk provider can and cannot do with the data.
* *Argument (B) - Kiosk provider as a controller*: The business / Central Legal have acknowledged that the API Integration Agreement is not the best fit for this initiative, but we are pushing ahead with it for the pilot phase in the interests of ‘getting this done’. I understand that under the API Integration setup, the business customer (i.e., the kiosk provider) would be an independent controller (this is how they are classified under the Bolt Business T&Cs), so we can proceed on that basis. However, since this setup is on shaky foundations, my concern is that it will be adopted ‘as standard’ in future, even though the data processing roles may not be a good fit for this setup.
{panel}

Ultimately, given the direction that the wind is blowing, I suppose {color:#36b37e}*we can go for the usual Bolt Business arrangement here*{color} (i.e., controller-to-controller / data sharing agreement) in the interests of keeping things streamlined and getting this done. In which case, my question for you would be this - {color:#4c9aff}*Have you finalised the Data Sharing Agreement in the updated* {color}[{color:#4c9aff}+*API Addendum*+{color}|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1I4hfO6VtTKDG9necgATHzBUUTE0gTf9kzBNZ4wRyAA8/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.kmrojrdg2vf3]{color:#4c9aff}*, so that I can leverage it for the kiosk setup?*{color}

