Hi [~accountid:62a057be6a7b750068a28b0b] - I have taken a quick look from the privacy side and overall this giveaway is {color:#36b37e}*low risk*{color} from my POV. Nevertheless, *I recommend the following*:

* We should make some amendments to clause 7 to avoid relying consent as a legal basis (unless strictly necessary).
* We should only be publishing strictly necessary information about the winners online / in our marketing channels.
* We should ensure that a link to the T&Cs are included in all giveaway comms.

I include further details below. Going forward, please ensure that the privacy team are looped in sooner, as a few hours for review is a very tight deadline (particularly when balanced against other competing priorities) 🕔 

I defer to the Legal Team for their comments 🙂 

----

{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}
*T&Cs* ([link|https://sites.google.com/bolt.eu/bolt-gb/gb-drivers-scheduled-rides-amazon-vouchers-giveaway])
{panel}

We should {color:#4c9aff}*make the following edits*{color} to the T&Cs:

{quote}*Clause 7.2*: _By accepting the Prize, Winners_ +*_agree_*+ _to the Giveaways Terms and Conditions._ +*_Winners acknowledge that Bolt will publish or make_*+ _available his/her name, likeness, image and/or voice (including photograph and video recording of the same) and country in Bolt’s website and any other marketing channels, including social media channels and newsletters,_ +*_as necessary to fulfill the these Special Terms and Conditions_*+_._ +*_Alternatively, in jurisdictions where consent is the only lawful basis for processing, we will rely on the Winner’s consent._*+ _Bolt may be required to provide the Winner’s information and winning entry to a regulatory authority on request. It is a condition of accepting the Prize that a Winner may be required to sign a legal release in a form to be determined by Bolt in its absolute discretion._”{quote}

* +Rationale+: If we rely on _consent_ as the legal basis for publishing the winners' details online (which is how the clause was originally drafted), the winners would have the right to withdraw that consent at any time. Given that this giveaway is fundamentally a marketing initiative (and so relies on Bolt being able to publicise the winners' details), we do not want to find ourselves in a situation where a winner withdraws their consent before we get a chance to publish their details. I have therefore updated the clause so that we are not primarily relying on consent as the legal basis here.

{quote}*Clause 7.4*: “_If you object to any or all of your_ +*_name_*+_, country and winning entry being published or made available, please contact us by emailing_ [+_giveaways.uk@bolt.eu_+|mailto:giveaways.uk@bolt.eu]_,_ +*_and such request will be considered in accordance with applicable requirements_*+_. Bolt must still provide the information and winning entry to the Advertising Standards Authority on request_.”{quote}

* +Rationale+: We are not always required to honour objection requests - there are exceptions under privacy law that we can try and rely on. As such, I have updated the clause to make this clear to  drivers. 

{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}
*Publishing details of the winners*
{panel}

(?) As a question - *What specific details abut the winners do we intend to publish online*?

* We should only publish information about winners that is {color:#4c9aff}*strictly necessary*{color} (or explicitly required by law). For example, I note from Clause 7.2 of the T&Cs that we may publish the winner’s photo - is this strictly necessary? To the extent that any information is not necessary, I recommend: (i) {color:#4c9aff}*not including this in the publicity materials*{color}; and (ii) {color:#4c9aff}*updating Clause 7* {color}to accurately state what information about the winners we will be publishing online / via our marketing channels.

{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}
*Giveaway comms*
{panel}

Please ensure that a {color:#4c9aff}*link to the T&Cs*{color} is included in all comms that we send to drivers promoting the giveaway.

* +Rationale+: The T&Cs include key information about the giveaway (including privacy language / a link to the privacy notice) that we should be providing to drivers upfront.

